# Keep the spec in sync

Whenever you change behaviour, architecture, auth, APIs, data model, configuration,
deployment, or iOS/server UX in this repo, update
[`specs/003-receipt-submission/spec.md`](../../../specs/003-receipt-submission/spec.md)
in the **same change**. It lives in the repository root alongside the specs for
the rest of the accounting stack; `docs/SPEC.md` is now only a pointer to it.

- Treat that spec as the source of truth for how the system works *as built*.
- Its numbered sections (§1–§12) are the detailed behaviour; user stories and
  requirements sit above them. Update whichever the change actually affects —
  a behaviour change usually touches a numbered section, and sometimes an
  acceptance scenario or FR too.
- Prefer editing the relevant section over appending a changelog.
- Remove obsolete claims (do not leave “formerly…” cruft unless it explains a
  deliberate design choice that still matters).
- If `README.md` duplicates the same operator-facing detail, update that too.
- Do not wait to be asked — updating the spec is part of finishing the task.
